Qt PDF: finish only outlines that emitted a subpath

QPdf::Stroker resets first before stroking and moveToHook clears it only
when a coordinate is written. An all-gap dashed outline emits no coordinates;
closing and filling it otherwise generates a PDF closepath without a current
point. Preserve every coordinated outline, fill and background operation.

Qualification patch for QtBase 6.11.2; not applied by the FreeCAD build.
Apply with -p1 in qt-everywhere, or -p2 in a standalone qtbase source tree.
Original Qt source licensing is preserved.

--- a/qtbase/src/gui/painting/qpdf.cpp
+++ b/qtbase/src/gui/painting/qpdf.cpp
@@ -655,3 +655,4 @@
     stroker->strokePath(path, this, cosmeticPen ? matrix : QTransform());
-    *stream << "h f\n";
+    if (!first)
+        *stream << "h f\n";
 }
